# Cursor Rules - Novel Hunter

Read and strictly follow [AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md).

## Critical Directives:
1. MANDATORY RULE: "Cada vez que agregues una feature, haz tests, corre los tests, actualiza la documentación de todo y luego commit."
2. ALWAYS update documentation in README.md and docs/ for every feature.
3. NEVER commit without running and passing:
   `npm test`
   `node test/test_db.js`
3. Architecture:
   - Frontend: Vanilla JS (ESM) + Electron Context Isolation (`preload.cjs`).
   - Database: SQLite 3NF via `node:sqlite`. Keep canonical chapters in `chapters` and translations in `chapter_translations` (`en`, `es`).
   - Packaging: Never write inside `app.asar`. Use `resolveStorageDir()` in `src/config.js`.
4. UI Consistency:
   - Screen headers must match menu button names exactly ("Buscador", "Mi biblioteca", "Consola Terminal", "Configuración").
   - Action buttons must maintain unified 36px height.
   - SVG vector icons only (no broken emojis).
   - 4 selectable themes in Settings aligned with app icon (`neon-hunter`, `deep-violet`, `midnight-velvet`, `slate-indigo`).
   - Button harmonization: No hardcoded hex colors (`#334155`, `#3b82f6`) on buttons or controls. Always use theme CSS variables (`var(--primary-gradient)`, `var(--accent-glow)`, `var(--bg-card)`, `var(--border-color)`, `var(--border-focus)`).
